{
  "title": "Nonunion and Bone Defects",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/basic-science/9069/nonunion-and-bone-defects",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jul 7 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Introduction",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A nonunion is an arrest in the fracture repair process",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "progressive evidence of non healing of a fracture of a bone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "a delayed union is generally defined as a failure to reach bony union by 6 months post-injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "this also includes fractures that are taking longer than expected to heal (ie. distal radial fractures)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "large segmental defects",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "should be considered functional non-unions",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "multifactorial",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "most commonly, inadequate fracture stabilization and poor blood supply lead to nonunion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "infection",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "eradication needs to occur along with the achieving fracture union",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "smoking",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "location",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "scaphoid, distal tibia, base of the 5th metatarsal are at higher risk for nonunion because blood supply in these areas",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "pattern",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "segmental fractures and those with butterfly fragments",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "increased risk of nonunion like because of compromise of the blood supply to the intercalary segment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Types of nonunion",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**septic nonunion**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "caused by infection",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "CRP test as the most accurate predictor of infection",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**pseudoarthrosis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**hypertrophic nonunion**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "caused by inadequate stability with adequate blood supply and biology",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "abundant callous formation without bridging bone",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "typically heal once mechanical stability is improved",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**atrophic nonunion**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "caused by inadequate immobilization and inadequate blood supply",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**oligotrophic nonunion**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "produced by inadequate reduction with fracture fragment displacement",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "important to discern injury mechanisms, non operative interventions, baseline metabolic, nutritional or immunologic statuses and use of NSAIDs and/or nicotine containing products",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "assess pain levels with axial loading of involved extremity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "important to complete a thorough neurovascular exam, including the status of the soft tissue envelope",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "assess mobility of the nonunion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "assess extremity for the presence of deformity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Laboratory evaluation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "CBC, ESR, CRP",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "must rule out infectious etiology",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "total protein and serum albumin",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "vitamin D, TSH, PTH",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Vitamin D deficiency is the most commonly encountered nutritional deficiency (60-70%)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "plain radiographs are the cornerstone for evaluation of fracture healing; four views should be included",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "full length weight bearing films should obtained if a limb length discrepancy is present",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "if the status of union is in question, a CT scan should be obtained; hardware artifact may limit utility of the CT scan",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "fracture brace immobilization",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "bone stimulators",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "contraindications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "synovial pseudoarthroses",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "mobile nonunions",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "greater than 1 cm between fracture ends",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "infected nonunion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "often associated with pseudoarthrosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "chance of fracture healing is low if infection isn't eradicated",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "staged approach often important",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "modalities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "need to remove all infected/devitalized soft tissue",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "use antibiotic beads, VAC dressings to manage the wound",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "with significant bone loss, bone transport may be an option",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "muscle flaps can be critical in wound management with soft tissue loss",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pseudoarthrosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may be found in association with infection",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "modalities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "removal of atrophic, non-viable bone ends",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "internal fixation with mechanical stability",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "maintenance of viable soft tissue envelope",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "hypertrophic nonunions",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "often have biologically viable bone ends",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "issue with fixation, not the biology",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "modalities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "internal fixation with application of appropriate mechanical stability",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "oligotrophic nonunions",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "often have biologically viable bone ends",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "may require biological stimulation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "modalities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "internal fixation with improved mechanical properties",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "atrophic nonunions",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "often have dysvascular bone ends",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "modalities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "need to ensure biologically viable bony ends are apposed",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "fixation needs to be mechanically stable",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "bone grafting",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "autologous iliac crest (osteoinductive) is gold standard",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "BMPs",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "osteoconductive agents (ie. crushed cancellous chips, DBM)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "establishment of healthy soft tissue flap/envelope",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Bone stimulators",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "four main delivery modes of electrical stimulation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "direct current",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "decrease osteoclast activity and increase osteoblast activity by reducing oxygen concentration and increasing local tissue pH",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "capacitively coupled electrical fields (alternating current, AC)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "affect synthesis of cAMP, collagen and calcification of carilage",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "pulsed electromagnetic fields",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "cause calcification of fibrocartilage",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "combined magnetic fields",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "bone simulators work through induction coupling, which stimulates bone growth through the following direct effects",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "increasing expression of BMP7 increasing expression of BMP7",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "increasing expression of BMP2",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "increasing expression of TGF-beta1",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "increasing expression of osteoblasts proliferation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
